// S6: Medium 3D grid, field reversal — adaptive DOPRI5
// Grid 300×300×6 → FFT 600×600×12 (IDENTICAL for CS and mumax3 since 2N)
// Same SP#4 Field A physics but 3D multi-layer: stiff switching + larger FFT cost/step
// Hypothesis: CS advantages compound (step count reduction × VkFFT speed/step)
// Fair: both DOPRI5, MaxErr=1e-4 (mumax3) ↔ rtol=1e-4 (CS), f32

SetGridSize(300, 300, 6)
SetCellSize(3e-9, 3e-9, 4e-9)
Msat  = 860e3
Aex   = 13e-12
alpha = 0.02
setsolver(5)           // DormandPrince (DOPRI5)
MaxErr = 1e-4
m = uniform(1, 0.1, 0.01)
B_ext = vector(-24.6e-3, 4.3e-3, 0)   // SP#4 Field A [Tesla]
run(3e-10)             // 0.3 ns (field reversal completes, then plateau)
